IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wills-making`
IMPORT `wills-qa`

-- Wills Act 1970 (WA) -- cases for the Q&A layer (wills-qa.l4): every exported question, for every role and every
-- situation.
--
-- Each question is asked for each role it is not about, with every other input an ASSUMEd value that has none: the
-- answer must be `does not arise for you`, and reading any of those inputs would stop the evaluation. Each question that
-- takes a situation input is asked, for its own role, with the value under which the situation does not hold and every
-- input after it ASSUMEd. For the baseline's seat (the will-maker and the beneficiary) the answers are also asserted
-- equal to the baseline's own export on the same facts. Expected values are worked by hand from the deposited text (the
-- quotations in wills-making.l4). The lives' facts are those of the baseline's cases (c025, c082, c087, c096, c098,
-- d074, d085, k084); the dates of Graham's and Giuseppe's wills (1 June 2040) are hypothetical, as there. A living
-- will-maker is asked as at 20 October 2026.
--
-- Generated by gen_wills.py in the session scratchpad. BASELINE. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Cases -- the Q&A layer`

ASSUME `an unasked fact` IS A BOOLEAN
ASSUME `an unasked number` IS A NUMBER
ASSUME `an unasked date` IS A DATE
ASSUME `an unasked provision` IS A Provision
ASSUME `an unasked marriage event` IS A `What happened to my marriage`
ASSUME `an unasked act` IS A `What I did`
ASSUME `an unasked route` IS AN `Another route to a valid will`

`as the will-maker` MEANS `I am making a will, or have made one`
`as the beneficiary or family` MEANS `I am named in the will of someone who has died, or am their family`
`as the witness` MEANS `I have been asked to witness a will, or have witnessed one`

