-- What becomes of this gift
-- Everything to a spouse who survives: takes effect (c087, k084); who dies first: not disposed of; half to a child who died first leaving a child: to that child's children (s 27, c098); half to a childless child who died first: accrues (s 26(1)(g)); a legacy to a friend who died first: residue (s 26(1)(b)); the will providing otherwise: as it provides.
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift takes effect as it is written`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift answer` (`What becomes of the gift in my will` (`the gift from` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it is not disposed of by the will (intestacy, under the Administration Act 1903)`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `it passes to the beneficiary's children who survive the will-maker, in equal shares`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the gift answer` (`What becomes of the gift in my will` (`the gift from` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `the share accrues to the other shares`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS `the gift falls into the residue`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE EQUALS `as the will itself provides for this case`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the will-maker` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `What becomes of this gift` `as the witness` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Do I take my parent's gift
-- My parent, the will-maker's child, died first with an outright gift: I take it (s 27); as a joint tenant: not (s 27(3)); the will saying otherwise: not; my parent not the will-maker's issue: not.
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS `yes if` (`Do the beneficiary's children take the gift under section 27` (`the gift from` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE))
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the will-maker` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Do I take my parent's gift` `as the witness` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Does the Act give me a share the will left out
-- Jake, left out of his father's will (k084): the Act gives no share; that is the Family Provision Act 1972.
#ASSERT `Does the Act give me a share the will left out` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Act give me a share the will left out` `as the beneficiary or family` TRUE EQUALS `yes if` (`Does this Act give me a share the will does not` TRUE)
#ASSERT `Does the Act give me a share the will left out` `as the beneficiary or family` FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Does the Act give me a share the will left out` `as the will-maker` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Does the Act give me a share the will left out` `as the witness` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- May I witness this will
-- s 11: a beneficiary who can see may witness; one who cannot see may not.
#ASSERT `May I witness this will` `as the witness` TRUE TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `May I witness this will` `as the witness` FALSE FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `May I witness this will` `as the will-maker` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `May I witness this will` `as the beneficiary or family` `an unasked fact` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`

-- Is our witnessing of the will enough
-- Two of us together, signing in the will-maker's presence: enough; one of two unable to see: not; three, one unable to see: enough; signing after the will-maker left: not (s 8(c), (d), s 11).
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the witness` 2 0 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the witness` 2 1 TRUE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the witness` 3 1 TRUE EQUALS yes
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the witness` 2 0 FALSE EQUALS no
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the will-maker` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
#ASSERT `Is our witnessing of the will enough` `as the beneficiary or family` `an unasked number` `an unasked number` `an unasked fact` EQUALS `does not arise for you`
